// T5 / S12.11: Pierce (Shift+G): "a point/curve and an edge crossing the sketch plane." Onshape:
// "Constrain a sketch entity to be coincident with the intersection point of its sketch plane
// and an arbitrary curve that is not in its sketch plane." A 40 × 30 box, 20 high, centred on
// the origin, so its edges along Y cross the Front plane. Sketch 2 on Front has two lines. Tool
// first: Shift+G, click the first line's end, then hover the box's top-right edge (it
// highlights, with the pierce point marked where it crosses the plane) and click it: the end
// jumps there, fixed, with a light-blue pierce glyph. Selection first: select the other line's
// end, Shift+G, click the top-left edge.
Scenario(
    start: Some("document"),
    steps: [
        WaitFor("document-shell"),
        Wait(30),
        Click(ui("sketch")),
        WaitFor("sketch-dialog"),
        Wait(3),
        Click(ui("feature-top")),
        Wait(3),
        Key("N"),
        Wait(40),
        Key("G"),
        Wait(2),
        ClickWorld(-20, -15),
        MoveWorld(20, 15),
        Wait(2),
        ClickWorld(20, 15),
        Wait(3),
        Type("40"),
        Key("Enter"),
